## Run by Octave when this directory joins the load path, which CleeCode arranges through
## OCTAVE_PATH on every shell it starts. That is the whole point: the workspace panel and the
## captured figures used to depend on the preset's own `--eval cleecode_boot`, so an Octave
## started any other way — typed at a shell tab, or launched by the Run button on a .m file —
## got none of it, and its plots opened in real windows behind the terminal.
##
## cleecode_boot returns immediately when CLEECODE_OCTAVE_WS is unset, so a copy of this
## directory on somebody's path outside CleeCode is inert rather than surprising.
cleecode_boot ();
